":true,"_score_accruals":45.8,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.05446708386714551,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":98.7,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.008452850822672359,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":0.38527165236081423,"_gp_spread":true,"_score_spread":100.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.2150454611720296,"_gp_roic_consistency":true,"_score_roic_consistency":64.2,"_gate_incr_roic":1.0,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.08239075145293503,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":60.8,"_gate_pool_share":0.1280529881009449,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":91.2,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.2189277205916984,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":0.009253248923878138,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":59.3,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.2635518852235714,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.009539842873176206,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":84.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.01623,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":10.8,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":["paper"],"description_full":"BellRing Brands, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides various nutrition products in the United States. The company offers ready-to-drink (RTD) protein shakes, other RTD beverages, protein powders, nutrition bars, and other products primarily under the Premier Protein and Dymatize brands. It distributes its products through club stores, food, drug and mass retailers, e-commerce, online and specialty retailers, and convenience stores channels. BellRing Brands, Inc. was incorporated in 2019 and is headquartered in Saint Louis, Missouri.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael  Axelrod | President, CEO & Director | Age 57","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 530 people. Revenue per employee of $4.4M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Defensive peers, improving at 19%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $483K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $42K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["BellRing Brands, Inc. is a small-cap consumer defensive business with a $1.1B market cap on $2.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +19% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 46% against a 7% cost of capital \u2014 a 39-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 33%.","The business throws off $256M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 11 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.21\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 5.2\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.9\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Consumer Defensive peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Slow-motion taste and channel shifts \u2014 private label, Gen-Z health preferences, or a DTC disruption can erode decade-old brand moats without a single dramatic quarter.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Input cost inflation from agricultural commodities \u2014 when raw materials spike, pass-through pricing lags and margin compression is immediate.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 8% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 86% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 33% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Consumer Defensive peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Growing faster than most Consumer Defensive peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 11% over 3 months","Consumer Defensive ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Trading the Move, Not the Narrative: (BRBR) Edition","s